[36m(TaskRunner pid=228462)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=228462)[0m We can simplify this expression further:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=228462)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=228462)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=228462)[0m R(\theta) = 300\cos\theta - 468\sin\theta + 24(\cos^2\theta + \sin^2\theta) + 48\sin^2\theta = 300\cos\theta - 468\sin\theta + 24 + 48\sin^2\theta
[36m(TaskRunner pid=228462)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=228462)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=228462)[0m To maximize \(R(\theta)\), we can use calculus to find the critical points. Let's take the derivative of \(R(\theta)\) with respect to \(\theta\) and set it to zero:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=228462)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=228462)[0m \[
