[36m(TaskRunner pid=228462)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=228462)[0m Let's represent \(z\) in its polar form. Since \(|z| = 4\), we can write \(z = 4e^{i\theta} = 4(\cos\theta + i\sin\theta)\). Therefore, \(\frac{1}{z} = \frac{1}{4}e^{-i\theta} = \frac{1}{4}(\cos\theta - i\sin\theta)\).
[36m(TaskRunner pid=228462)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=228462)[0m Now we can substitute \(z\) and \(\frac{1}{z}\) into the expression:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=228462)[0m 
